{
  "program": "CBTRN02C",
  "caseId": "case18",
  "description": "THE DECLARATIVE PROOF OF THE POSTING ORDER, and the case that shows '22' is fatal here. TRANFILE is seeded with a record already carrying TRAN-ID 0000000000683580 - the very identifier dailytran row 0 will be posted under - so the keyed add at :564 reports the duplicate status '22'. 2900-WRITE-TRANSACTION-FILE enumerates no duplicate arm: :566 accepts '00' and nothing else, so :569 moves 12 and :574-577 display 'ERROR WRITING TO TRANSACTION FILE', render the status and abend. Because '22' is numeric and its first character is not '9', 9910 takes its :722-725 arm instead of the extended one and the line reads FILE STATUS IS: NNNN0022 - the same paragraph, the other branch, which is why this case and case14 belong together. What makes it the order proof is what survives: 2700-UPDATE-TCATBAL ran at :440 and 2800-UPDATE-ACCOUNT-REC at :441, both BEFORE the write that failed, so the category balance comes back at +504.77 and the account at 697.77 with cycle credit 504.77 while the transaction master still holds only its seed. Reverse the three PERFORMs and this case cannot pass. Every dataset in this program is RECOVERY(NONE) and the program issues no syncpoint, so those two writes are durable and the abend does not take them back.",
